---A face annotation object contains the results of face detection.
---@class gcp.vision_v1.FaceAnnotation
---@field surpriseLikelihood? gcp.vision_v1.FaceAnnotationSurpriseLikelihoodEnum Deprecated: No longer populated.
---@field detectionConfidence? number Detection confidence. Range [0, 1].
---@field panAngle? number Yaw angle, which indicates the leftward/rightward angle that the face is pointing relative to the vertical plane perpendicular to the image. Range [-180,180].
---@field underExposedLikelihood? gcp.vision_v1.FaceAnnotationUnderExposedLikelihoodEnum Under-exposed likelihood.
---@field tiltAngle? number Pitch angle, which indicates the upwards/downwards angle that the face is pointing relative to the image's horizontal plane. Range [-180,180].
---@field rollAngle? number Roll angle, which indicates the amount of clockwise/anti-clockwise rotation of the face relative to the image vertical about the axis perpendicular to the face. Range [-180,180].
---@field boundingPoly? gcp.vision_v1.BoundingPoly The bounding polygon around the face. The coordinates of the bounding box are in the original image's scale. The bounding box is computed to "frame" the face in accordance with human expectations. It is based on the landmarker results. Note that one or more x and/or y coordinates may not be generated in the `BoundingPoly` (the polygon will be unbounded) if only a partial face appears in the image to be annotated.
---@field angerLikelihood? gcp.vision_v1.FaceAnnotationAngerLikelihoodEnum Deprecated: No longer populated.
---@field landmarkingConfidence? number Face landmarking confidence. Range [0, 1].
---@field joyLikelihood? gcp.vision_v1.FaceAnnotationJoyLikelihoodEnum Deprecated: No longer populated.
---@field landmarks? gcp.vision_v1.LandmarkList Detected face landmarks.
---@field headwearLikelihood? gcp.vision_v1.FaceAnnotationHeadwearLikelihoodEnum Headwear likelihood.
---@field fdBoundingPoly? gcp.vision_v1.BoundingPoly The `fd_bounding_poly` bounding polygon is tighter than the `boundingPoly`, and encloses only the skin part of the face. Typically, it is used to eliminate the face from any image analysis that detects the "amount of skin" visible in an image. It is not based on the landmarker results, only on the initial face detection, hence the fd (face detection) prefix.
---@field sorrowLikelihood? gcp.vision_v1.FaceAnnotationSorrowLikelihoodEnum Deprecated: No longer populated.
---@field blurredLikelihood? gcp.vision_v1.FaceAnnotationBlurredLikelihoodEnum Blurred likelihood.

